Mitcad's patch to OCCT 8.0.1, under OCCT's licence:
SPDX-License-Identifier: LGPL-2.1-only WITH OCCT-exception-1.0

Fillets: a rounding ending where its wall steps back into the material by
much less than the radius (mitcad#343).

The case: a rim's edge rounded with 0.3 up to a vertex where the rim's
wall steps back by 4.3 micrometres; the wall's face at the edge ends on a
strip that narrow (the step's face, square to the rounding), beyond which
the wall goes on in the stepped-back plane. The bodies stored in the files
end the rounding at the section through the vertex and close it with a
quarter torus: the ball turns on about its contact's end point on the
strip's edge until it lies in the wall's plane, the torus cut by the
stepped-back wall.

- ChFi3d_Builder::PerformPivotAtStepEnd (new, tried first for the end of
  a lone stripe in PerformFilletOnVertex): where the contact on a plane Fs
  ends on its edge with a plane strip narrower than a tenth of the radius,
  the face beyond the strip parallel to Fs and the strip's width into the
  material, the other face a plane square to Fs and to the edge: the
  stripe ends at the section through the vertex (a free end), and a corner
  stripe of one piece, the torus about the contact's end point on the
  axis along the other face's normal (both radii the rounding's), closes
  it: its contacts are its cut by the stepped-back face (computed) and the
  circle on the other face. The transitions follow from the side each face
  keeps, seen along the normal of its surface. Before, OCCT found no face
  for the end and left an invalid shape.
- ChFi3d_Builder::Compute (after the stripes are in the data structure):
  the end section of such an end becomes two edges, the one over the strip
  bounding it, the other the torus's; the strip has the first.

On the design's body before the item, the rounding of the rim's edges
(the item's 14 edges): valid, every face on the stored body's (distance 0
both ways), the change of volume -1.7315 against the file's -1.7477 mm3;
before, the result was invalid. Synthetic: a block's edge rounded
with 0.3 up to a step back of 0.0043, below and above, one rim and both,
as built and mirrored: valid, a quarter torus at each end, the material
taken within 2e-6 mm3 of the integral; before, the shape was invalid.

Upstream: new.
